# uAthena map-server load monitor - crontab example
# Install:
#   1) ensure MongoDB 7 (+ mongosh) and the mysql/mariadb client are present
#   2) edit /opt/uathena/bin/cron/uamon.conf (Mongo URI/DB, SQL creds, retention)
#   3) run ONCE:   /opt/uathena/bin/cron/uamon-init.sh      (creates indexes)
#   4) install this crontab:   crontab -e   (paste the lines below)
#
# Paths assume `make install` copied scripts/cron -> /opt/uathena/bin/cron/.
# The per-minute job runs for ~CPU_SAMPLE_SECS each minute (the CPU delta window).

# every minute: raw snapshot (CPU busiest-thread / RAM / players-per-map)
* * * * *    /opt/uathena/bin/cron/uamon-minute.sh  >> /opt/uathena/log/uamon.log 2>&1

# every 10 minutes: aggregate the last 10 min (avg + peak)
*/10 * * * * /opt/uathena/bin/cron/uamon-10min.sh   >> /opt/uathena/log/uamon.log 2>&1

# every hour (at :00): aggregate the last hour (avg + peak)
0 * * * *    /opt/uathena/bin/cron/uamon-hour.sh    >> /opt/uathena/log/uamon.log 2>&1

# --- monthly (1st of each month) -----------------------------------------
# 01:00 - rebalance per-instance map lists (confN/maps_athena.conf) from peaks
0 1 1 * *    /opt/uathena/bin/cron/uamon-autoconf.sh >> /opt/uathena/log/uamon.log 2>&1
# 02:00 - restart the map-servers so the new map lists take effect
#         (supervisor restarts every instance; replace with your own restart if any)
0 2 1 * *    systemctl restart uAmap.service          >> /opt/uathena/log/uamon.log 2>&1
# 04:00 - purge stats past their retention window
0 4 1 * *    /opt/uathena/bin/cron/uamon-cleanup.sh   >> /opt/uathena/log/uamon.log 2>&1
